WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.984 --> 00:00:12.666
- [Mark] All right, Maddie.

00:00:12.666 --> 00:00:14.430
Maddie, where'd you grow up?

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:15.990
Where are you from originally?

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:17.340
- [Maddie] Um, I've grown up

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:19.640
in a couple of different states,

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:22.743
Arizona, Oregon, Wyoming, and here.

00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:24.463
- [Mark] Tell me about your childhood.

00:00:24.463 --> 00:00:26.617
You had both your parents
when you were a child?

00:00:26.617 --> 00:00:29.740
- Um, I didn't have a childhood really.

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:33.131
I was always getting left places

00:00:33.131 --> 00:00:34.920
by my biological parents,

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:36.820
so when I was taken from them

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:39.610
foster care and getting
adopted wasn't really good.

00:00:39.610 --> 00:00:44.340
And then the adoption
family, (car engine revving)

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:48.120
and I kind of got really on bad terms,

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:49.173
and I came out here.

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:53.480
- [Mark] How'd your
biological parents lose you?

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:56.240
- Um, my mom's a drug
addict and a prostitute.

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:58.503
And then my dad is in prison.

00:00:58.503 --> 00:01:01.280
- [Mark] So you went to the
foster system at what age?

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:02.113
- Five.

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:05.632
- [Mark] How was that experience?

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:06.540
- It wasn't good.

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:08.331
I just went to one home.

00:01:08.331 --> 00:01:11.150
The first day I went to one home

00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:12.490
and then they didn't want us,

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:14.026
so then I went to the next home.

00:01:14.026 --> 00:01:17.355
That home ended up adopting
us two years later,

00:01:17.355 --> 00:01:22.090
and until I was 12 I lived with them,

00:01:22.090 --> 00:01:24.823
before I went to mental health hospitals.

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:28.240
After that I was sent
to live with my brother

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:29.440
'cause he was my only option.

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:32.670
And I didn't know him before
I went to go live with him.

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:34.033
And then I came out here.

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:36.510
- [Mark] How was the time

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:38.122
you spent with your brother?

00:01:38.122 --> 00:01:39.701
- It was okay.

00:01:39.701 --> 00:01:43.710
It was better than being at
home with the foster parents,

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:45.710
but it wasn't the best,

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:47.560
but it was still better.

00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:49.860
- [Mark] Any abuse when you were a kid?

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:51.350
- Yeah, I have had sexual abuse

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:54.420
and physical abuse and emotional abuse.

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:55.720
- [Mark] From the foster parents?

00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:56.553
- Yeah.

00:01:58.060 --> 00:02:00.340
- [Mark] What age was that going on?

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:02.307
- From eight years old

00:02:02.307 --> 00:02:07.160
all the way up until I was 15

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:09.577
I was getting abused by the mom.

00:02:09.577 --> 00:02:11.203
She'd hit me,

00:02:14.590 --> 00:02:16.960
and she'd always say
that she didn't love me

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:18.710
or other stuff.

00:02:18.710 --> 00:02:23.710
And the dad, in third grade
he started sexual abuse,

00:02:24.787 --> 00:02:28.783
abusing until I was in seventh grade.

00:02:32.712 --> 00:02:35.803
- [Mark] And then you went
on your own at what age?

00:02:36.910 --> 00:02:38.570
- 15.

00:02:38.570 --> 00:02:39.884
- [Mark] Where'd you go?

00:02:39.884 --> 00:02:41.120
- Out here.

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:41.953
- [Mark] To LA?

00:02:44.876 --> 00:02:46.903
You've been homeless since when?

00:02:48.158 --> 00:02:51.273
- June 24, 2019.

00:02:53.309 --> 00:02:54.840
- [Mark] So you had a job for awhile?

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:55.960
- No.

00:02:55.960 --> 00:02:56.810
- [Mark] How old are you?

00:02:56.810 --> 00:02:57.871
- I'm 16 and a half.

00:02:57.871 --> 00:02:59.693
- [Mark] Oh, you're 16?

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:04.120
You look older.

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:06.720
- Yeah, I get that a lot.

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:08.413
- [Mark] I would not have
guessed you to be 16.

00:03:11.850 --> 00:03:13.990
So you have mental health issues as well?

00:03:13.990 --> 00:03:16.830
I mean, it's hard not to
with the childhood you had.

00:03:16.830 --> 00:03:17.663
- Yeah.

00:03:17.663 --> 00:03:21.250
I tried everything possible
to get out of the house,

00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:23.680
'cause I couldn't take it anymore.

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:26.688
I couldn't stay there and
keep getting hit or abused.

00:03:26.688 --> 00:03:29.830
And it was really starting to weigh on me

00:03:29.830 --> 00:03:31.170
so I started cutting myself,

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:33.460
and I overdosed when I was 12.

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:34.993
I had a whole bunch of pills,

00:03:36.850 --> 00:03:38.900
like eight, nine different kind of pills,

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:46.700
and social workers in
Oregon didn't do anything

00:03:47.550 --> 00:03:49.293
'cause they deemed the house safe.

00:03:53.390 --> 00:03:55.210
- [Mark] So did you go
to high school at all?

00:03:55.210 --> 00:03:56.840
- Yeah, I went to the first year

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:58.343
of high school, ninth grade,

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:01.100
and I'm a little above ninth grade,

00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:05.873
but other than that I
haven't continued back up.

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:08.480
- [Mark] Where do you stay now?

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:09.313
You're in a tent?

00:04:09.313 --> 00:04:10.146
- Yeah.

00:04:12.017 --> 00:04:14.435
- [Mark] Are you using drugs at all?

00:04:14.435 --> 00:04:18.150
- Sometimes I do, but I've looked up a lot

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:20.080
and seen a lot of people change on it,

00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:23.712
and the new drug, that
fentanyl that came out ages.

00:04:23.712 --> 00:04:25.820
I'm starting to slow down,

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:27.158
but sometimes I relapse.

00:04:27.158 --> 00:04:27.991
- [Mark] So you're using fentanyl?

00:04:27.991 --> 00:04:29.580
- Because I get bored.

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:30.809
Oh no, I don't use fentanyl.

00:04:30.809 --> 00:04:32.390
- [Mark] What do you use?

00:04:32.390 --> 00:04:33.654
- Most of the time I use crystal,

00:04:33.654 --> 00:04:35.260
and I smoke it.

00:04:35.260 --> 00:04:37.813
I used to shoot it up, but
I almost died from that.

00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:40.950
- [Mark] Are you using any other drugs,

00:04:40.950 --> 00:04:42.224
heroin or crack?

00:04:42.224 --> 00:04:43.663
- I used heroin one time,

00:04:43.663 --> 00:04:45.688
it was not my drug.

00:04:45.688 --> 00:04:48.540
And I used crack one time,

00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:50.323
but I didn't feel anything from it.

00:04:52.170 --> 00:04:53.250
- [Mark] How are you supporting yourself?

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:54.550
What do you do for money now?

00:04:54.550 --> 00:04:55.586
- Recycling.

00:04:55.586 --> 00:04:58.600
I also have family out here.

00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:02.130
And they're not like my blood family,

00:05:02.130 --> 00:05:03.550
they're just people I've met out here

00:05:03.550 --> 00:05:08.163
who have watched over me
and taking care of me.

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:15.670
- [Mark] Have you had any
bad things happen to you

00:05:15.670 --> 00:05:17.413
while you've been down here on skid row?

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:21.646
You seem like you might be a
little more vulnerable target

00:05:21.646 --> 00:05:23.580
than most folks.

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:26.006
- Yeah, people, like
just 'cause I'm white,

00:05:26.006 --> 00:05:27.925
that makes me a target.

00:05:27.925 --> 00:05:29.889
And people are really racist out here.

00:05:29.889 --> 00:05:32.170
Even them being adults.

00:05:32.170 --> 00:05:33.810
I like, not being rude,

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:37.060
I'm more of an adult than
a lot of people out here

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:39.390
because they like to start drama,

00:05:39.390 --> 00:05:41.240
and it's just entertainment for them.

00:05:42.290 --> 00:05:43.910
I've been sexually abused out here.

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:46.593
- [Mark] What kind of
stuff has happened here?

00:05:47.940 --> 00:05:50.990
- Guys touching me in my sleep.

00:05:50.990 --> 00:05:52.263
Some guys cumming on me.

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:55.410
I had a boyfriend,

00:05:55.410 --> 00:05:58.093
my first boyfriend who
used to me up every day.

00:06:00.980 --> 00:06:01.998
- [Mark] Do you find yourself doing things

00:06:01.998 --> 00:06:04.753
outside of what you'd
normally allow yourself to do

00:06:04.753 --> 00:06:06.393
since you've been down here?

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:10.700
- [Maddie] I think the only
thing is really smoking,

00:06:10.700 --> 00:06:15.700
and maybe eating food that
I wouldn't normally eat

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:18.827
on an everyday basis,

00:06:18.827 --> 00:06:23.827
but being out here has made
me also become more grown

00:06:26.316 --> 00:06:29.610
because I see how people are,

00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:33.399
and I did not want to be my
final resting spot out here,

00:06:33.399 --> 00:06:35.000
but...

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:36.620
- [Mark] You still have
hope for a better life?

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:37.453
- [Maddie] Mm-hmm.

00:06:37.453 --> 00:06:38.286
- [Mark] That's good.

00:06:38.286 --> 00:06:41.903
- [Maddie] But I know that the
foster care system is not my,

00:06:43.269 --> 00:06:46.290
it's not the right choice for me,

00:06:46.290 --> 00:06:48.940
so I know if I could
just push through this

00:06:48.940 --> 00:06:51.700
until I could just make it till I'm 18,

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:55.860
and then do online school and
get an SRO and then get a job.

00:06:55.860 --> 00:06:57.064
- [Mark] That'd be great.

00:06:57.064 --> 00:06:59.690
You know, 'cause you don't
seem to fit down here.

00:06:59.690 --> 00:07:00.523
- [Maddie] No.

00:07:00.523 --> 00:07:02.840
- You don't seem to be meant for this.

00:07:02.840 --> 00:07:04.120
- [Maddie] But at the same time

00:07:04.120 --> 00:07:06.603
I have people who make me fit in.

00:07:07.874 --> 00:07:10.460
They just support,

00:07:10.460 --> 00:07:11.750
they don't like me being down here,

00:07:11.750 --> 00:07:15.187
but they always have
my back and everything.

00:07:15.187 --> 00:07:17.280
It's a family out here.

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:19.050
- [Mark] Yeah, getting
away from this neighborhood

00:07:19.050 --> 00:07:21.150
would probably be a healthy thing for you.

00:07:23.276 --> 00:07:26.273
- I, I don't know if I could do that

00:07:26.273 --> 00:07:29.459
because of people out here
who I've connected with

00:07:29.459 --> 00:07:31.310
who are good for me,

00:07:31.310 --> 00:07:34.890
but at the same time that's the only part

00:07:34.890 --> 00:07:35.723
that would scare me,

00:07:35.723 --> 00:07:37.593
I would never be able to see them again.

00:07:40.176 --> 00:07:41.460
- [Mark] Do you feel like this life

00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:43.833
on skid row is a good fit for you?

00:07:45.548 --> 00:07:47.840
I mean a lot of people feel

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:50.930
like this is their home, eventually.

00:07:50.930 --> 00:07:51.940
- It's home.

00:07:51.940 --> 00:07:52.773
It is home.

00:07:54.214 --> 00:07:57.463
It does grow on you,
but everybody hates it.

00:07:58.670 --> 00:08:01.460
The gangbangers, they all hate it,

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:03.611
and they regret going into the gangs,

00:08:03.611 --> 00:08:07.110
but they still do it because
once you're in a gang

00:08:07.110 --> 00:08:10.745
you can't really go backwards.

00:08:10.745 --> 00:08:13.270
And it's really hard,

00:08:13.270 --> 00:08:16.683
like there will be days where it rains

00:08:16.683 --> 00:08:18.860
and there's no food.

00:08:18.860 --> 00:08:21.800
You go five days without food,

00:08:21.800 --> 00:08:23.483
soaking wet with no clothes,

00:08:24.610 --> 00:08:27.550
but it'll all come to you eventually.

00:08:27.550 --> 00:08:29.740
Depends on what your hustle is.

00:08:29.740 --> 00:08:32.020
A lot of people hustle,

00:08:32.020 --> 00:08:36.913
and they hoe or they sell
drugs or kill people.

00:08:37.870 --> 00:08:40.943
It all depends on the person.

00:08:43.130 --> 00:08:45.010
- [Mark] When were you
first introduced to drugs?

00:08:45.010 --> 00:08:46.038
- Hmm?

00:08:46.038 --> 00:08:48.638
- [Mark] When did you first
get introduced to drugs?

00:08:51.113 --> 00:08:56.113
- 20, 28, 27th of June last year.

00:09:01.017 --> 00:09:04.980
Within the first month
I started shooting up,

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:08.843
and I did two back-to-back
shots and almost died from that.

00:09:11.210 --> 00:09:14.943
And that scared me enough
not to do shots anymore.

00:09:17.020 --> 00:09:18.740
- [Mark] Are you scared that maybe

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:22.920
if you spend too much time
down here you'll have changed?

00:09:22.920 --> 00:09:25.270
- I've changed a lot
since being down here.

00:09:25.270 --> 00:09:29.110
I've learned more about myself

00:09:29.110 --> 00:09:31.584
and things I didn't like like anger,

00:09:31.584 --> 00:09:36.080
but I guess that's a lot about being hurt.

00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:37.650
And I do put up with a lot,

00:09:37.650 --> 00:09:40.050
like I get a lot of bullying,

00:09:40.050 --> 00:09:44.685
and there's a lot of not
fitting in that it doesn't help.

00:09:44.685 --> 00:09:47.093
And people are scared because my age,

00:09:48.251 --> 00:09:53.251
but I have also changed in a good way too.

00:09:53.329 --> 00:09:57.403
I'm just scared that this place is,

00:09:57.403 --> 00:10:01.020
they don't want nobody to succeed,

00:10:01.020 --> 00:10:04.600
or you usually end up following the crowd,

00:10:04.600 --> 00:10:08.400
and I'm afraid that I might die out here

00:10:08.400 --> 00:10:09.390
if I'm not strong enough,

00:10:09.390 --> 00:10:11.570
or if I do the wrong mistake on accident

00:10:11.570 --> 00:10:13.451
because I'm mad or something.

00:10:13.451 --> 00:10:14.676
But other than that,

00:10:14.676 --> 00:10:16.983
I'm not really afraid of being out here.

00:10:17.860 --> 00:10:19.350
- [Mark] Are you afraid of

00:10:19.350 --> 00:10:21.450
maybe a changing your personality?

00:10:21.450 --> 00:10:23.717
You know, your values might change

00:10:23.717 --> 00:10:25.990
by being down here over time.

00:10:25.990 --> 00:10:26.823
- To a certain point-

00:10:26.823 --> 00:10:29.150
- [Mark] You might become
a harder, tougher version

00:10:29.150 --> 00:10:31.963
of the softer, kinder
girl that you once were.

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:35.640
- Yeah, to a certain point yes,

00:10:35.640 --> 00:10:37.760
but also it has opened my eyes

00:10:37.760 --> 00:10:40.163
because the world is a very cruel place.

00:10:41.739 --> 00:10:43.480
Everywhere is different,

00:10:43.480 --> 00:10:46.550
but it's also teaching me a lot

00:10:46.550 --> 00:10:49.150
to see right through
the bull shit of people,

00:10:49.150 --> 00:10:52.800
and lying and ulterior
motives that people have,

00:10:52.800 --> 00:10:56.745
'cause a lot of people tell you something

00:10:56.745 --> 00:10:59.240
to tell you it to get what they want

00:10:59.240 --> 00:11:02.926
out of the situation instead
of what is best for you,

00:11:02.926 --> 00:11:06.600
and the saying that you are born alone

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:08.960
and you die alone is very true,

00:11:08.960 --> 00:11:11.740
but you can't live life alone.

00:11:11.740 --> 00:11:14.034
You can't also rely on everybody a lot.

00:11:14.034 --> 00:11:15.140
- [Mark] All right, Maddie,

00:11:15.140 --> 00:11:16.020
well thank you for coming in

00:11:16.020 --> 00:11:17.769
and talking with me.

00:11:17.769 --> 00:11:20.570
Good luck with getting out of skid row

00:11:20.570 --> 00:11:21.707
and getting your life together.

00:11:21.707 --> 00:11:23.270
It would be really nice to see you

00:11:23.270 --> 00:11:25.130
find somebody that
takes you away from here

00:11:25.130 --> 00:11:27.053
and get your life back on track.

00:11:28.737 --> 00:11:32.010
- [Maddie] If there was a
chance I could get schooling

00:11:32.010 --> 00:11:36.190
and still be out here and
my SRO and a job legally,

00:11:36.190 --> 00:11:37.023
I'd do all of it,

00:11:37.023 --> 00:11:39.248
but just live on my own

00:11:39.248 --> 00:11:41.810
so I could get a real apartment

00:11:41.810 --> 00:11:43.309
instead of an SRO.

00:11:43.309 --> 00:11:45.459
- [Mark] All right,
Maddie, well good luck.

00:11:46.880 --> 00:11:48.259
I wish the best for you.

00:11:48.259 --> 00:11:49.407
- Thank you.

